      "message": "Not blocking: `install: false` leaves the `commit-message` check with no `hk` on a cache miss.\n\nWhat shows it: with `install: false` the step only restores the mise cache. When the cache key changes (a `bin/mise` or config version bump) and the matrix runs only `commit-message` (a patch set touching nothing the checks read), the restore misses, nothing installs `hk`, and `mise exec -- hk run commit-msg` fails. Previously `bin/mise install` with the job\u0027s empty `MISE_ENV` installed `hk` alone.\n\nFix: drop the `install:` line; the job\u0027s `MISE_ENV: \u0027\u0027` already limits the install to `hk`, which is cheap.",
